## Cycle summary

This cycle worked the PROGRAM.md NEXT ACTION on **open item 4 (census entropy constant)** and delivered a clean method-closure plus a correction of a prior cycle.

**What I built** (extended `experiments/analytic/local_pattern_census/census_entropy_asymptotic.py`):
- **`_jc_vec`** — numpy-vectorised joint-cover engine, multi-limb uint64 (N>64), largest-head-batched-via-doubling so no head prime falls into a 2^h Python loop. ~10× faster (2²⁶ block: 204s → ~20s), bit-for-bit equal to the reference.
- **`joint_cover_int` / `lnP_miss_exact`** — exact big-integer engine (each I-E term `= sign·∏(2^{n_w}−1)` since `excl+Σn_w=N`); numerator `== count_tm` exactly, zero floating cancellation.
- **`--bracket-sweep`** — measures the rigorous bracket width vs the I-E cost budget.
- A noise-floor guard on the float `P_miss` (returns `None` instead of garbage past reliability).
- Selftests grew 11 → **14 groups** (vec==py multi-limb; sweep monotonicity/plateau/shut; exact==count_tm + the precision wall), all green.

**Findings:**
